@chapter 29 | Biology Miscellaneous

@intro
The closing chapter gathers a wide mix of life-science questions: **recent Nobel work** and science policy, **health programmes and days** (Mission Indradhanush, NACO, AIDS Day), **body chemistry** (cholesterol, trans fat, antioxidants, dehydration), **microbes and fermentation**, **medical devices and specialists** (EEG, endoscope, pacemaker, heart transplant), **animals** (breeds, three-chambered hearts, pheromones, bioluminescence), **plants and agriculture** (herbicides, eutrophication, tree rings, Green Revolution) and a long list of **research institutes**, many of them in Uttar Pradesh. It contains **{pyqs} PYQs and {ones} one-liners**.
@end

